WEBVTT

00:57.432 --> 00:59.642
- Here. Look at the numbers.
- No.

00:59.726 --> 01:00.935
- They're wrong.
- Hey.

01:01.019 --> 01:02.312
- Look.
- It's heading south.

01:02.395 --> 01:04.564
I mean, look.

01:04.647 --> 01:07.108
It's moving to Japan. It's on here.

01:07.192 --> 01:09.235
- No.
- If not, the damage will be too great.

01:09.319 --> 01:12.113
It's descending from the north.
It's moving down,

01:12.197 --> 01:14.616
so it's flowing this way right now.

01:14.699 --> 01:16.201
- Do the numbers say that?
- Look.

01:16.284 --> 01:17.368
What?

01:20.205 --> 01:21.081
Hey.

01:21.164 --> 01:23.583
Hey, look at this.
This is the current data.

01:24.209 --> 01:25.376
It's flowing this way.

01:25.460 --> 01:28.338
This is up there.

01:47.148 --> 01:49.150
TYPHOON RICKY CONTINUES TO
CAUSE DAMAGE IN VARIOUS LOCATIONS

01:49.234 --> 01:51.152
- Jeez.
- Okay.

01:51.236 --> 01:52.904
- Sir.
- Yes?

01:54.656 --> 01:58.284
Hi. Get the estimated precipitation again.

01:58.368 --> 02:00.286
- Okay.
- Yes?

02:06.876 --> 02:08.128
Please take a look at this.

02:11.548 --> 02:12.549
Okay.

02:15.093 --> 02:16.678
Hi, this is Chief Team One.

02:16.761 --> 02:17.720
Yes.

02:30.108 --> 02:33.278
Last night, the 14th Typhoon Ricky
swept the Korean Peninsula,

02:33.361 --> 02:35.697
making the entire country a mess.

02:35.780 --> 02:37.574
There were about 120 casualties

02:37.657 --> 02:39.742
due to strong winds of 30m per second.

02:39.826 --> 02:43.413
The amount of property damage alone
is estimated to exceed 80 billion won.

02:44.038 --> 02:48.126
Heavy rain that fell overnight
caused flooding across the country.

02:48.209 --> 02:50.253
Early this morning,
in Yangcheon-gu, Seoul,

02:50.336 --> 02:52.547
- a four-lane road was flooded
- The KMA got it this time.

02:52.630 --> 02:53.923
and drainage work was carried out.

02:54.007 --> 02:55.842
- Ha-kyung will be criticized less.
- An underground

02:55.925 --> 02:57.969
shopping mall in Suncheon was flooded.

02:58.052 --> 02:59.596
Yes, that's right.

03:00.430 --> 03:04.684
This typhoon did not deviate much
from our predicted scenario.

03:04.767 --> 03:08.438
- Yes. The precipitation and the path
- We live with multiple scenarios.

03:08.521 --> 03:10.273
of the typhoon were almost identical.

03:11.316 --> 03:12.567
Thank you.

03:13.151 --> 03:14.360
Yes.

03:15.904 --> 03:19.198
TYPHOON'S PREDICTED PATH CLOSELY MATCHES
WITH THE FORECAST OF THE KMA

03:22.243 --> 03:26.456
Sometimes, the scenario
you prepared proves right.

03:32.045 --> 03:33.087
Excuse me.

03:33.713 --> 03:36.090
I need to use the bathroom.

03:42.013 --> 03:44.599
Why are we bringing him?

03:45.808 --> 03:47.268
This is the best I can do…

03:50.480 --> 03:53.358
to mend Si-woo's relationship with his dad

03:54.234 --> 03:55.485
and with me.

04:05.620 --> 04:07.080
Some things in this world

04:07.705 --> 04:09.749
are just impossible.

04:10.500 --> 04:13.378
Just like how humans
can't change a typhoon's course,

04:13.461 --> 04:15.755
the same goes
for my relationship with my father.

04:16.798 --> 04:18.216
It can never

04:18.841 --> 04:20.134
be changed.

04:22.762 --> 04:24.764
I stay true to myself

04:25.348 --> 04:27.267
just like you do.

04:32.480 --> 04:33.982
I'm sorry

04:34.816 --> 04:36.693
that this is all I'm worth.

04:39.862 --> 04:41.072
Let's…

04:43.157 --> 04:44.367
break up.

04:55.545 --> 04:58.214
If the expected scenario goes off course,

04:59.549 --> 05:02.385
it can lead to the worst outcome.

05:07.640 --> 05:09.309
So you didn't come here to see me.

05:10.893 --> 05:11.728
Well…

05:17.442 --> 05:18.443
Yu-jin.

05:33.249 --> 05:34.667
The important thing is that

05:35.168 --> 05:38.046
whether the scenario you prepared
is right or wrong,

05:38.129 --> 05:39.922
life goes on.

05:40.006 --> 05:43.259
You know that
the 15th typhoon is coming, right?

05:44.010 --> 05:45.887
It looks like…

05:45.970 --> 05:47.472
- Eight hours?
- Yes.

05:47.555 --> 05:50.600
In eight hours,
it'll enter the Korean Peninsula.

05:50.683 --> 05:54.729
There's no need to return to Seoul.
Stay there and check the second one.

05:54.812 --> 05:55.897
What?

05:56.647 --> 05:59.067
Where do you think?

05:59.150 --> 06:01.611
You have to go to the typhoon center.

06:02.195 --> 06:05.740
- Go right now.
- Pardon? Now?

06:06.365 --> 06:08.034
Wait, sir. I--

06:14.665 --> 06:16.334
And we have to prepare

06:17.210 --> 06:20.838
for the next scenario
and the scenario after that.

06:27.178 --> 06:33.184
EPISODE 13
SCENARIO 1, 2, 3

06:51.619 --> 06:53.079
When did you find out?

06:53.162 --> 06:54.247
Well…

06:55.748 --> 06:56.916
It's been a while.

07:00.002 --> 07:00.962
What?

07:08.761 --> 07:10.847
That long ago?

07:11.973 --> 07:13.975
What about you? When did you find out?

07:14.058 --> 07:17.395
It's been a while since I had a hunch.

07:24.652 --> 07:26.362
Forecaster Lee, did you catch a cold?

07:26.446 --> 07:27.405
Yes.

07:27.488 --> 07:30.241
We'll begin the morning meeting of May 10.

07:30.324 --> 07:31.451
Satellite center--

07:32.994 --> 07:34.078
I'm sorry.

07:35.288 --> 07:36.372
Now…

07:37.039 --> 07:38.416
Thank you.

07:43.880 --> 07:46.048
Gosh, I got goosebumps.

07:46.132 --> 07:48.885
Since then? I got chills just now.

07:50.011 --> 07:51.304
When did you find out?

07:51.888 --> 07:53.473
I found out later.

07:54.098 --> 07:55.475
Remember that day?

08:18.831 --> 08:21.334
Right. It was so obvious.

08:21.959 --> 08:23.628
I couldn't pretend I didn't know.

08:23.711 --> 08:25.129
I caught them too many times.

08:30.760 --> 08:33.137
Get it together, Forecaster Lee!

08:33.721 --> 08:34.722
Yes, ma'am.

08:34.805 --> 08:37.099
They should have taken it easy.

08:39.769 --> 08:42.480
Anyway, what are we going to do?

08:43.064 --> 08:45.066
What can we do other than play innocent?

08:45.566 --> 08:49.028
We'll continue to keep our mouths shut
and pretend we don't know.

08:51.072 --> 08:52.782
Pretend you don't know what?

08:54.742 --> 08:57.370
- What?
- What is it? Why?

08:57.870 --> 08:59.872
Why did you stop talking?

08:59.956 --> 09:01.749
It's nothing.

09:16.305 --> 09:18.224
Senior Forecaster Um
probably knows, right?

09:18.307 --> 09:20.768
Of course. He lived with them.

09:20.851 --> 09:22.853
If he doesn't know,
then he must be really dense.

09:22.937 --> 09:23.771
What?

09:26.983 --> 09:28.192
Did you talk about me?

09:28.693 --> 09:29.610
What?

09:29.694 --> 09:30.695
No.

09:30.778 --> 09:32.154
- No.
- No.

09:33.531 --> 09:36.033
Jeez. You found out so fast.

09:37.159 --> 09:39.412
That's right. I'm about to be divorced.

09:47.795 --> 09:49.839
How did they find out?

09:53.718 --> 09:57.597
Sir, I only have 6,000 won.

09:58.222 --> 10:00.474
Could you please drive me to the airport?

10:00.558 --> 10:02.518
Please? Come on.

10:02.602 --> 10:04.478
Excuse me. Hey!

10:05.229 --> 10:06.397
You…

10:09.025 --> 10:10.693
Jeez.

10:13.821 --> 10:16.115
Damn it.

10:20.953 --> 10:22.288
Jeez.

10:26.125 --> 10:27.543
Hey, Ms. Director.

10:28.794 --> 10:30.671
Let me ask you a question.

10:32.715 --> 10:35.885
Why did you have to drag me
all the way here

10:35.968 --> 10:38.471
knowing that Si-woo
wouldn't be happy to see me?

10:40.556 --> 10:41.974
I have a question too.

10:42.558 --> 10:44.060
Your son is hurt.

10:44.143 --> 10:45.811
How can you
only talk about the settlement?

10:47.938 --> 10:50.566
The world is after you
to take the shirt off your back.

10:50.650 --> 10:52.276
If you're naive,

10:52.360 --> 10:54.320
you can never survive.

10:54.403 --> 10:56.530
As a father, I need to stay alert

10:56.614 --> 10:58.783
and take all I can get.

11:00.034 --> 11:01.869
Is that wrong?

11:02.828 --> 11:06.040
There are so many
different kinds of fathers.

11:12.088 --> 11:15.132
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

11:38.489 --> 11:40.533
Some fathers work hard,

11:41.117 --> 11:44.870
but they always feel sorry
towards their children.

11:45.496 --> 11:49.667
Some irresponsible fathers take flight

11:50.459 --> 11:52.378
and leave their young children behind.

11:53.671 --> 11:57.967
And some fathers are shameless and
selfish when it comes to their children.

12:00.678 --> 12:01.929
Jeez.

12:02.012 --> 12:03.389
Damn it!

12:04.014 --> 12:05.599
I shouldn't have come here.

12:14.191 --> 12:15.943
You'll have to return to Seoul alone.

13:08.746 --> 13:11.415
Get in. I'll drive you to your mother's.

13:14.543 --> 13:17.296
I have something to say. Please get in.

14:18.607 --> 14:22.361
Why did you send
a director from Headquarters here?

14:22.444 --> 14:24.238
I don't think she'll be of much help.

14:25.489 --> 14:27.908
I have to follow your orders,
Director General.

14:27.992 --> 14:29.410
Yes, sir.

14:33.163 --> 14:35.833
Currently, Typhoon Elisha has
a central pressure of 985

14:35.916 --> 14:37.585
and a maximum wind speed of 27

14:37.668 --> 14:40.921
and has moved northward
to the sea about 250km south of Jeju.

14:41.005 --> 14:42.673
With that size and speed,

14:42.756 --> 14:44.925
it's likely to land on the southern coast.

14:45.009 --> 14:46.802
I'll analyze the path.

14:46.886 --> 14:49.054
You can be in charge
of the synoptic weather observation.

14:49.972 --> 14:50.931
Got it?

14:51.557 --> 14:52.516
Okay.

14:52.600 --> 14:54.518
SYNOPTIC WEATHER OBSERVATION: OBSERVATIONS
MADE AT A SPECIFIC TIME AT ALL STATIONS

14:54.602 --> 14:56.228
How is Forecaster Lee?

14:57.646 --> 14:58.939
The burn treatment is over,

14:59.023 --> 15:01.108
but his eyes need
to be monitored for a while.

15:01.817 --> 15:03.068
Is that so?

15:05.487 --> 15:08.157
A person got hurt,
but you seem indifferent.

15:14.455 --> 15:18.959
Are you making a fuss
because I let your colleague get hurt?

15:20.711 --> 15:22.504
No, I just think

15:22.588 --> 15:26.634
you should show some concern at least.

15:30.763 --> 15:31.972
Director Jin.

15:32.765 --> 15:36.060
You've only worked at Headquarters, right?

15:36.143 --> 15:37.227
Yes. And?

15:40.105 --> 15:41.482
Do you know how I got this?

15:43.651 --> 15:46.362
I slipped while going up to Baengnokdam

15:46.445 --> 15:48.364
to check the AWS there.

15:51.408 --> 15:54.495
Assistant Director Park can't hear
with his left ear well.

15:55.079 --> 15:58.457
Because he was hit by a signboard
on site during a storm.

15:59.959 --> 16:02.419
On his way to observe the wind field,

16:02.503 --> 16:04.254
Mr. Jung Su-hwan's car rolled over.

16:06.882 --> 16:09.635
Anyone who has worked in the field
for more than ten years

16:09.718 --> 16:11.762
has at least one wound like this.

16:11.845 --> 16:13.764
I'm sorry about Forecaster Lee's injury,

16:13.847 --> 16:15.683
but it happens every day here.

16:17.017 --> 16:19.019
Do you get it, Director Jin?

16:21.563 --> 16:22.523
Yes.

16:23.190 --> 16:24.024
Director?

16:26.026 --> 16:27.444
I'm the director here.

16:28.153 --> 16:29.738
- Please look at this.
- Okay.

16:49.925 --> 16:51.051
What?

16:51.969 --> 16:53.679
You should be in the hospital.

16:55.472 --> 16:58.058
They said I didn't get hurt
as much as they thought.

16:58.142 --> 17:00.310
Besides, I recover fast.

17:00.394 --> 17:01.770
I heard you hurt your eyes.

17:01.854 --> 17:04.857
They said I just need to monitor them
for a few days.

17:04.940 --> 17:07.234
Everything's fine so far.

17:11.030 --> 17:13.115
Did you hear that, Director Jin?

17:27.212 --> 17:28.797
I need to talk to you.

17:48.859 --> 17:51.153
I can't do this anymore.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.655
Just be a man and sign the divorce papers.

17:53.739 --> 17:55.157
Let's get a divorce

17:55.240 --> 17:57.201
and live carefree lives

17:57.910 --> 17:59.995
like we do right now, okay?

18:17.471 --> 18:19.056
What do you think of this?

18:21.391 --> 18:23.310
JIN TAE-KYUNG

18:31.777 --> 18:33.153
It's cute.

18:37.074 --> 18:39.409
SAVE

18:48.460 --> 18:51.839
- Is the typhoon report ready yet?
- Pardon? Yes.

18:54.174 --> 18:56.760
- The typhoon report is being uploaded.
- Okay.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.808
See you after work.

19:09.606 --> 19:12.151
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:14.319 --> 19:15.863
Su-jin, I need to see you.

19:20.075 --> 19:21.201
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

19:22.953 --> 19:24.079
Okay.

19:25.581 --> 19:27.499
I have to go to the Policy Office.

19:27.583 --> 19:28.584
Okay.

19:32.129 --> 19:34.256
GYEOL'S HOMEROOM TEACHER

19:34.339 --> 19:37.176
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

19:38.594 --> 19:40.470
Yes, ma'am. Hello.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.599
Did Gyeol do that?

19:44.349 --> 19:47.352
Yes. He does that sometimes.

19:47.936 --> 19:48.896
Goodness.

19:49.855 --> 19:51.690
Yes. Really?

19:52.191 --> 19:55.485
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:55.569 --> 19:57.196
Go back to the hospital right now.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.448
I already got discharged.

19:59.531 --> 20:02.075
And I have no problem working.

20:04.828 --> 20:06.622
Do you always have it your way?

20:09.499 --> 20:10.459
Let's…

20:11.126 --> 20:12.586
break up.

20:18.091 --> 20:20.344
Do you think you can end it like that?

20:20.928 --> 20:22.930
Sure. You said what was on your mind.

20:23.680 --> 20:25.474
But I haven't given you an answer.

20:26.099 --> 20:27.726
So wait until I do.

20:30.395 --> 20:32.773
Director Jin. Please come to the office.

20:38.153 --> 20:41.323
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

20:42.199 --> 20:43.408
What's that?

20:43.992 --> 20:45.244
That's what I want to ask.

20:46.495 --> 20:47.663
What is that?

20:50.999 --> 20:53.502
Seok-ho, what's that
on the typhoon report window?

20:53.585 --> 20:55.963
The typhoon report? What about it?

21:05.931 --> 21:07.516
What?

21:08.100 --> 21:09.851
What's a penguin doing there?

21:14.022 --> 21:15.148
Assistant Director Shin.

21:15.232 --> 21:17.150
Did you upload that?

21:25.367 --> 21:26.868
What are you doing? Take it down!

21:28.203 --> 21:30.455
Yes… Yes, sir.

21:36.044 --> 21:37.337
TYPHOON REPORT

21:38.505 --> 21:41.008
A typhoon is about to hit.

21:41.550 --> 21:43.093
Who's responsible for this?

21:43.176 --> 21:46.430
Not even a rookie here
would make a mistake like that.

21:49.391 --> 21:50.475
Is it Assistant Director Shin?

22:00.277 --> 22:02.029
Yes, it's me. What happened?

22:03.238 --> 22:04.448
Well…

22:05.365 --> 22:06.616
Assistant Director Shin

22:07.284 --> 22:09.661
uploaded the wrong file.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.538
It's all my fault.

22:12.205 --> 22:13.665
It happened while I was gone.

22:15.208 --> 22:16.376
I'm not sure.

22:16.460 --> 22:18.712
I don't know what that penguin is.

22:19.296 --> 22:21.298
I wonder where it came from.

22:32.267 --> 22:34.186
Senior Forecaster Um,
please get yourself together.

22:34.269 --> 22:37.105
When I'm gone, you're the acting director.

22:38.648 --> 22:41.943
Everyone's excited because we got
the path of the 14th typhoon.

22:42.027 --> 22:43.361
Number 15 is about to hit.

22:43.445 --> 22:45.655
I'm sorry. I have no excuse.

22:45.739 --> 22:46.740
What…

22:46.823 --> 22:48.617
Please be understanding, Director Jin.

22:49.201 --> 22:51.745
Senior Forecaster Um is beside himself.

22:52.287 --> 22:55.749
His wife might divorce him.

22:56.875 --> 22:58.168
What?

22:58.251 --> 23:00.921
Exactly. He's distracted.

23:01.004 --> 23:03.381
I should have paid more attention.

23:03.465 --> 23:05.092
It's all my fault, Director Jin.

23:05.175 --> 23:06.635
Why would you tell her that?

23:06.718 --> 23:09.930
- What if she's on speakerphone?
- No, it's my fault, Director Jin.

23:10.013 --> 23:11.181
- Assistant Director Shin?
- Well…

23:11.264 --> 23:13.850
I made a terrible mistake
when a typhoon is approaching.

23:13.934 --> 23:16.937
This shouldn't have happened.

23:17.020 --> 23:20.941
It's all my fault. I'll write an apology.

23:21.024 --> 23:22.609
- No.
- If that's not enough,

23:22.692 --> 23:24.111
have my salary reduced.

23:24.194 --> 23:25.195
- Come on.
- What are you saying?

23:25.278 --> 23:27.447
- No, it's my fault, Director Jin.
- Never mind.

23:27.531 --> 23:28.907
- I should have checked.
- No.

23:28.990 --> 23:30.700
- Stop it. It's my fault.
- No, it isn't.

23:30.784 --> 23:32.994
No, Senior Forecaster Um
is about to be divorced.

23:33.078 --> 23:34.955
- Ms. Oh, then--
- Come on.

23:35.038 --> 23:36.581
- One at a time.
- Director Jin.

23:36.665 --> 23:37.874
- Please talk one at a time.
- Yes.

23:37.958 --> 23:40.168
- One at a time, please.
- It was my fault.

23:45.632 --> 23:46.633
Yu-jin!

23:47.801 --> 23:50.303
- Don't run. You'll fall.
- Ki-jun is here.

23:51.304 --> 23:52.347
Ki-jun?

24:01.439 --> 24:02.816
Why are you here?

24:03.525 --> 24:05.735
I told you I had something to say.

24:07.863 --> 24:08.905
Hi.

24:08.989 --> 24:10.657
- You're here.
- Ma'am.

24:10.740 --> 24:12.701
Oh, yes. Thanks.

24:12.784 --> 24:14.786
Yu-jin, go inside and eat this.

24:14.870 --> 24:16.955
I have to get groceries for dinner.

24:17.038 --> 24:18.123
It's okay.

24:18.748 --> 24:22.460
You came all the way here,
so I'll make you dinner.

24:22.544 --> 24:23.545
Okay?

24:26.548 --> 24:27.716
Yu-jin.

24:33.722 --> 24:36.558
I don't know what happened,
but you should comfort her.

24:37.225 --> 24:40.353
She usually doesn't get mad like that.

24:40.437 --> 24:41.479
Right.

24:47.944 --> 24:49.487
My wife wants a divorce.

24:50.030 --> 24:51.406
Out of the blue?

24:54.284 --> 24:56.620
I don't think it was out of the blue.

24:58.038 --> 24:59.581
So what did you tell her?

25:00.165 --> 25:01.249
I couldn't say much.

25:01.333 --> 25:02.792
Will you get a divorce?

25:03.960 --> 25:07.088
She asked me not to give her a hard time.

25:07.589 --> 25:10.383
She suffered all her life because of me.

25:10.467 --> 25:11.968
Clinging to her now

25:12.552 --> 25:15.138
will make her suffer more, I think.

25:16.556 --> 25:18.308
You need to change her mind.

25:18.975 --> 25:20.977
How can I change her mind?

25:21.061 --> 25:23.230
Persuade her or explain yourself.

25:23.313 --> 25:24.397
Come up with a plan.

25:24.481 --> 25:25.565
A plan?

25:26.983 --> 25:28.735
Don't you know Scenario 1, 2, 3?

25:36.368 --> 25:37.994
Why did you come all the way here?

25:38.828 --> 25:40.622
I came to see you, of course.

25:41.248 --> 25:42.874
I had to do something

25:42.958 --> 25:44.501
because I don't want to break up.

25:44.584 --> 25:47.462
What will you do?
Is there anything left to do?

25:55.470 --> 25:57.722
- Ki-jun.
- I'm sorry, Yu-jin.

25:58.723 --> 26:01.393
I'm sorry I hurt you and made you upset.

26:02.143 --> 26:03.311
It's all my fault.

26:04.187 --> 26:05.355
What are you doing?

26:06.189 --> 26:07.315
Get up.

26:10.402 --> 26:11.486
I said get up.

26:11.569 --> 26:13.446
Come to Seoul with me, Yu-jin.

26:15.073 --> 26:16.074
Get up.

26:16.157 --> 26:18.827
If you say yes, I'll get up.

26:28.336 --> 26:29.629
- Get up.
- No.

26:30.171 --> 26:31.214
Answer me first.

26:31.298 --> 26:33.550
Yes, okay, so get up.

26:33.633 --> 26:34.843
Really?

26:34.926 --> 26:36.886
You'll come to Seoul with me then?

26:36.970 --> 26:38.013
Okay, so get up.

26:40.348 --> 26:41.558
Goodness.

26:57.824 --> 26:59.617
I admit that it was my fault,

26:59.701 --> 27:01.911
but I can't tell you why it happened.

27:02.579 --> 27:03.496
I'm sorry.

27:03.997 --> 27:06.958
It's personal, so I can't tell you.

27:09.461 --> 27:13.465
My husband can't seem
to focus on studying.

27:14.132 --> 27:16.760
The exam is right around the corner.

27:18.136 --> 27:21.681
But my mother-in-law says
she can't babysit the kids anymore.

27:21.765 --> 27:23.350
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

27:23.433 --> 27:25.101
My wife wants a divorce.

27:30.231 --> 27:31.358
Let's…

27:33.526 --> 27:34.778
break up.

27:41.826 --> 27:44.287
What does the GDAPS show?

27:44.371 --> 27:46.373
GDAPS: GLOBAL DATA ASSIMILATION
AND PREDICTION SYSTEM

27:47.415 --> 27:50.460
It's moving faster
due to the influence of the upper jet.

27:50.543 --> 27:53.088
I checked the vertical wind shear
and it's over 50.

27:53.880 --> 27:54.964
Okay.

28:16.319 --> 28:18.488
Did you find out who made the mistake?

28:19.531 --> 28:20.490
Yes.

28:20.573 --> 28:23.326
What an embarrassing moment for the KMA.

28:24.369 --> 28:26.454
You make silly mistakes
because all you do is

28:26.538 --> 28:30.250
sit comfortably in a chair
and look at the situation room monitors.

28:32.794 --> 28:35.672
Haven't you ever made a mistake?

28:36.965 --> 28:38.508
People at the typhoon center

28:39.008 --> 28:41.052
work hard and get injured a lot

28:41.136 --> 28:43.221
because they work on site.

28:43.805 --> 28:45.098
I know that.

28:45.181 --> 28:47.475
But we go through a lot
at Headquarters too.

28:53.106 --> 28:56.151
There's someone
who is about to be divorced.

28:57.068 --> 28:58.945
From here to here.

28:59.446 --> 29:00.613
Oh, hold on.

29:01.781 --> 29:04.159
Hi, Mother. I'm sorry. I'm working.

29:04.242 --> 29:05.702
Hold on. Can you send it to me?

29:06.286 --> 29:07.328
I'm sorry.

29:08.329 --> 29:10.832
There's someone who has to work to death

29:10.915 --> 29:12.417
to support her family

29:12.500 --> 29:14.711
while making apologies every day.

29:14.794 --> 29:16.254
Yes, I'm sorry.

29:21.259 --> 29:24.387
There's someone who is too busy
to see the seasons change outside.

29:33.229 --> 29:34.522
And there's someone

29:34.606 --> 29:37.484
who is spending his youth
sacrificing his dating life for work.

29:41.237 --> 29:42.071
What?

29:42.155 --> 29:45.992
Are we trying to show off
who's having a harder time?

29:46.576 --> 29:47.494
No.

29:47.577 --> 29:50.330
I'm saying that the typhoon center
and the situation room at Headquarters

29:50.413 --> 29:53.208
are all doing the same hard work
within the KMA.

29:54.083 --> 29:56.669
So stop weighing the gravity of our work

29:56.753 --> 29:58.963
and taking sides, Director Sung.

30:08.264 --> 30:10.558
- Assistant Director Lee.
- Yes?

30:10.642 --> 30:13.353
- Bring me the predicted scenario.
- Yes, ma'am.

30:35.124 --> 30:37.377
Why are you here at this hour?

30:37.460 --> 30:38.586
Well…

30:40.296 --> 30:42.674
Give me some time, Hyang-rae.

30:43.591 --> 30:44.801
Give me three months.

30:44.884 --> 30:48.263
Let's have a grace period of three months.

30:49.347 --> 30:50.557
What do you mean?

30:50.640 --> 30:53.643
Honestly, I think this is really unfair.

30:53.726 --> 30:55.895
So for three months,

30:56.563 --> 30:59.065
let's try living like a family.

31:00.108 --> 31:03.027
Then I'll do whatever you want.

31:03.111 --> 31:05.405
If you ask me for a divorce,

31:05.488 --> 31:06.906
I'll comply.

31:06.990 --> 31:09.534
If you tell me
to get the hell out of Seoul, I will.

31:10.994 --> 31:12.912
Do you think that will change anything?

31:12.996 --> 31:14.330
Come on.

31:14.956 --> 31:17.375
Even prisoners on death row
have a grace period.

31:17.959 --> 31:22.255
Can't you at least give me that much time?

31:22.338 --> 31:25.216
You have to acknowledge
my dedication to this family.

31:29.095 --> 31:30.805
Why aren't you at work?

31:32.432 --> 31:34.726
It's lunchtime, so I ran here.

31:34.809 --> 31:37.562
Go back to work.
You don't want to be late.

31:37.645 --> 31:39.939
- Honey.
- Leave already.

32:46.297 --> 32:47.590
Yes, Hyang-rae.

32:48.091 --> 32:49.342
What's all this?

32:50.593 --> 32:51.678
What?

32:54.889 --> 32:56.391
That's…

32:56.975 --> 32:58.309
A typhoon is coming.

32:58.393 --> 33:01.187
This one will have strong winds.
So I put them up.

33:03.940 --> 33:04.983
Hello?

33:06.818 --> 33:07.819
Hyang-rae.

33:07.902 --> 33:10.196
I don't think
I can do it for three months.

33:11.322 --> 33:12.532
I see…

33:13.908 --> 33:15.118
Okay.

33:17.453 --> 33:18.746
I'll give you two months.

33:20.540 --> 33:21.666
Two months?

33:21.749 --> 33:24.335
Do whatever you want for two months.

33:24.919 --> 33:28.006
After two months,
you have to sign the divorce papers.

33:32.885 --> 33:36.055
Okay. Thanks, Hyang-rae.

33:37.348 --> 33:38.433
I'll really…

33:39.267 --> 33:40.393
I'll do my best.

33:45.481 --> 33:46.733
Hello?

33:48.317 --> 33:49.902
Thanks, Hyang-rae!

34:12.717 --> 34:13.843
All right.

34:17.388 --> 34:20.516
- It's new, so it's fluffy.
- Thank you.

34:21.267 --> 34:24.270
It's a little damp in here, isn't it?

34:24.353 --> 34:27.023
I should have turned on the heat.

34:27.106 --> 34:28.399
It's okay, Mother.

34:28.483 --> 34:31.235
Do you want me
to turn it on for a little bit?

34:31.319 --> 34:33.571
It's okay. We'll take care of it.

34:34.363 --> 34:36.074
- Okay.
- All right.

34:36.157 --> 34:37.909
- Good night.
- Okay.

34:37.992 --> 34:39.869
- Good night.
- All right.

34:39.952 --> 34:41.287
- Thank you.
- Good night.

34:56.803 --> 34:59.055
I told you to get a room at a motel.

35:01.933 --> 35:05.019
Your dad asked me to sleep here.
How could I?

35:05.686 --> 35:06.729
He's not my dad.

35:07.438 --> 35:09.315
A stepdad is still a dad, Yu-jin.

35:09.398 --> 35:10.858
Don't be like that to him.

35:11.567 --> 35:14.362
- What did I do?
- You were so curt.

35:14.445 --> 35:16.739
You didn't even look at him during dinner.

35:16.823 --> 35:18.616
You don't know anything.

35:18.699 --> 35:21.119
Right. I don't know anything.

35:21.911 --> 35:24.580
It's just that
you're making him walk on eggshells.

35:24.664 --> 35:27.166
That's why I hate him.
I hate him for doing that.

35:28.543 --> 35:30.336
He isn't like that
around Mom and Dong-jin.

35:31.129 --> 35:33.965
- It's because you--
- I know he's a good man.

35:34.048 --> 35:35.716
He cares about Mom.

35:35.800 --> 35:38.094
He's a good dad to Dong-jin,

35:38.177 --> 35:39.971
but there's no place for me here.

35:41.430 --> 35:43.850
It's Mom's family, not mine.

35:43.933 --> 35:46.686
That's why I wanted
to make my own family and…

35:46.769 --> 35:48.062
And?

35:50.606 --> 35:53.067
Never mind. Let's go to sleep.

35:53.151 --> 35:56.154
Why don't you want to
register our marriage?

35:58.489 --> 36:00.283
Do I have to repeat myself?

36:00.366 --> 36:02.201
How can I trust you?

36:02.285 --> 36:05.204
You're more worried about
what people think of us,

36:05.288 --> 36:07.123
who Ha-kyung is dating,

36:07.206 --> 36:10.168
and how that affects us.

36:10.251 --> 36:11.419
But it's…

36:12.753 --> 36:15.047
But it's Lee Si-woo of all people.

36:16.174 --> 36:17.008
So?

36:17.091 --> 36:19.510
What's bothering you the most? Be honest.

36:19.594 --> 36:21.345
The fact that I lived with Si-woo?

36:21.429 --> 36:23.556
Or that he's dating Ha-kyung?

36:24.140 --> 36:25.183
Both.

36:27.018 --> 36:28.811
I'm bothered by both. They upset me.

36:28.895 --> 36:30.730
So let's come up with a conclusion.

36:30.813 --> 36:32.648
There's no conclusion, Yu-jin.

36:33.232 --> 36:35.234
You and I are married.
That's our conclusion.

36:35.318 --> 36:36.694
So tell me if you regret it.

36:38.070 --> 36:39.238
You can take it back.

36:43.618 --> 36:45.244
Yu-jin, why are you doing this?

36:45.870 --> 36:48.706
I knelt down and apologized.
Why can't we move on?

36:48.789 --> 36:51.167
I'm sorry, but I can't live like you.

36:51.250 --> 36:54.670
I can't pretend to be lovey-dovey
or act like we have no problem.

36:54.754 --> 36:56.339
I don't want to be pretentious.

36:58.049 --> 36:59.926
I can't live like that.

37:00.009 --> 37:01.552
Do you think I like doing that?

37:01.636 --> 37:03.304
But everyone lives like that.

37:03.387 --> 37:05.014
Married couples do that.

37:05.097 --> 37:07.642
I don't care if everyone does.
I can't live like that.

37:07.725 --> 37:09.143
What do you want me to do?

37:09.227 --> 37:10.186
So…

37:11.270 --> 37:14.315
Why are you here giving me a hard time?

37:17.860 --> 37:19.028
- Honey.
- What?

37:19.111 --> 37:21.030
Did you make my daughter cry?

37:21.113 --> 37:22.448
- Honey.
- Sir, it's not what you think.

37:22.531 --> 37:23.574
- Come out.
- Goodness.

37:23.658 --> 37:24.992
- Sir.
- Come out!

37:25.076 --> 37:26.160
- Oh, goodness.
- Wait.

37:27.411 --> 37:28.246
You…

37:29.914 --> 37:31.249
- You jerk.
- Yes?

37:31.332 --> 37:33.209
Why did you make my daughter cry?

37:33.292 --> 37:35.127
Sir, it's not what you think.

37:35.211 --> 37:37.463
Honey, let go of him and talk.

37:37.546 --> 37:40.424
Hey, didn't I warn you before the wedding?

37:40.508 --> 37:44.053
I told you I'd kill you
if you made my daughter cry, didn't I?

37:44.136 --> 37:45.721
You did.

37:45.805 --> 37:46.973
But why did you make her cry?

37:47.056 --> 37:49.517
How long have you been married?

37:49.600 --> 37:51.310
It's only been a few months.

37:51.394 --> 37:53.187
How dare you make her cry already?

37:53.271 --> 37:54.647
- Why you--
- Dad! Stop it.

37:56.941 --> 37:58.025
What?

37:58.651 --> 37:59.777
"Dad"?

38:00.987 --> 38:02.154
I mean…

38:03.072 --> 38:04.657
What's wrong with you?

38:08.995 --> 38:11.455
This is our problem so you stay out of it.

38:14.208 --> 38:15.626
- Let's go inside.
- Okay.

38:17.586 --> 38:18.754
Okay.

38:24.135 --> 38:25.678
You heard it, right?

38:25.761 --> 38:28.014
She called me Dad, didn't she?

38:30.808 --> 38:34.145
Let's go inside.
It's their problem to take care of.

38:34.228 --> 38:36.564
- Let's go.
- She called me Dad.

38:36.647 --> 38:39.233
Okay. Let's go inside.

38:40.026 --> 38:41.068
Let's go.

38:52.872 --> 38:56.208
For now,
the first scenario is the most likely.

38:56.292 --> 38:58.377
Starting at the coast
of South Jeolla Province,

38:58.461 --> 39:00.254
it'll pass through the Korean Peninsula,

39:00.338 --> 39:03.382
cause damage nationwide,
and then exit through Pohang.

39:04.133 --> 39:07.553
The second scenario is
when it bends further to the east.

39:07.636 --> 39:09.972
There will be less damage than the former,

39:10.056 --> 39:13.267
but the southern regions within the radius
of the typhoon will be hit.

39:13.351 --> 39:14.852
What's the third scenario?

39:15.436 --> 39:17.521
As the North Pacific's
anticyclone contracts,

39:17.605 --> 39:21.317
it'll shift toward Kyushu along the edge
of the southern seas of Jeju.

39:21.400 --> 39:25.821
It'll only slightly affect some parts
of the southern coast and Busan.

39:26.822 --> 39:29.742
If the North Pacific's anticyclone
contracts a little more,

39:29.825 --> 39:32.953
will it bend more eastward
like in the second scenario?

39:34.497 --> 39:37.416
Given the current
North Pacific's anticyclone,

39:37.500 --> 39:39.251
that's very unlikely.

39:39.752 --> 39:41.087
Senior Forecaster Um.

39:41.170 --> 39:44.924
Is there any possibility that it'll weaken
by changing course to the south?

39:46.384 --> 39:48.094
Yes, there is.

39:48.177 --> 39:51.222
But there's also a possibility
that it'll move quickly to the east

39:51.305 --> 39:53.724
due to the northern jet stream.

39:54.850 --> 39:57.728
That means it could move to the east.

39:58.312 --> 40:00.648
Yes. We can be more accurate

40:00.731 --> 40:03.234
when the ground data comes in.

40:03.317 --> 40:05.444
Is there a way for us to know sooner?

40:07.822 --> 40:08.989
Well…

40:14.161 --> 40:16.163
We could launch a sonde
at the eastern side of Jeju

40:16.247 --> 40:18.457
- and at the sea west of the island.
- And?

40:19.083 --> 40:22.920
But I'm sure you know it's highly
dangerous in these weather conditions.

40:23.003 --> 40:26.382
But it's the best we can do
at the moment, right?

40:29.301 --> 40:30.719
Why don't we do this?

40:30.803 --> 40:33.722
Let's launch a sonde
only in the east Woljeong-ri area.

40:33.806 --> 40:35.474
There will be some errors,

40:35.558 --> 40:37.726
but it'll be better
than making a wild guess.

40:37.810 --> 40:39.228
Then I'll go do it at sea.

40:50.489 --> 40:51.782
Director Jin.

40:51.866 --> 40:53.659
Have you made any sonde observations?

40:54.243 --> 40:55.077
If you haven't,

40:55.161 --> 40:58.372
you won't be able to launch a sonde
in this weather.

40:58.956 --> 41:00.541
Director Jin. Listen carefully.

41:01.750 --> 41:04.587
There's no such thing
as an accurate forecast.

41:04.670 --> 41:07.131
Okay? We can only make predictions.

41:07.214 --> 41:08.757
You know what I mean?

41:09.508 --> 41:12.261
The 14th typhoon caused too much damage.

41:12.344 --> 41:14.597
We don't know how much more damage

41:14.680 --> 41:16.765
the upcoming Typhoon Elisha will cause.

41:16.849 --> 41:20.311
Even if they're just predictions,
I believe it is our duty to use

41:20.394 --> 41:22.813
the most accurate data possible
to make such predictions.

41:27.568 --> 41:29.653
We can't afford to
get it wrong this time, sir.

41:32.448 --> 41:35.493
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

41:52.009 --> 41:55.095
SEOUL, DOKDO, SEOGWIPO
OKINAWA, JAPAN

42:10.986 --> 42:11.862
Why are you coming?

42:11.946 --> 42:14.281
Do you think you can launch a sonde
just by heading out to sea?

42:14.907 --> 42:16.158
On a day like this,

42:16.242 --> 42:18.285
automatic observation may not work.

42:41.058 --> 42:45.229
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

44:08.395 --> 44:10.439
Weather Number One has arrived near Ieodo.

44:11.440 --> 44:13.025
We're ready.

44:13.609 --> 44:15.569
Let's float it at exactly 9 p.m.

44:15.653 --> 44:16.737
Okay.

44:17.655 --> 44:19.948
Director Jin. The winds are too strong.

44:20.032 --> 44:21.533
Automatic observation won't work.

44:22.117 --> 44:23.744
We'll have to do it manually.

44:27.414 --> 44:28.957
Can you do the countdown?

44:29.041 --> 44:30.250
Yes, okay.

45:05.411 --> 45:07.329
Five, four…

45:07.413 --> 45:08.330
Three…

45:09.540 --> 45:11.500
two, one!

46:23.071 --> 46:24.907
It worked. We're getting data.

46:38.629 --> 46:39.588
It's coming.

46:39.671 --> 46:41.256
We're getting
the Ieodo sea observation data.

46:41.340 --> 46:42.591
Are we?

46:49.681 --> 46:50.766
Okay.

46:53.435 --> 46:55.187
Yes. Did you get the observed value?

46:55.270 --> 46:56.813
We're feeding the data.

46:56.897 --> 46:58.398
We just need to check
the NWP model prediction data.

46:58.482 --> 47:00.984
When it's out, send it to me right away.

47:01.068 --> 47:02.027
Okay.

47:07.616 --> 47:09.284
Your prediction was right.

47:09.368 --> 47:11.870
At this rate,
it'll move along the Southern Sea

47:11.954 --> 47:14.122
and cause damage
in some southern regions only.

47:21.838 --> 47:23.423
Did you get the NWP model?

47:23.507 --> 47:25.133
Yes, I just saw it.

47:25.217 --> 47:27.344
We'll have to announce the course
as the South Sea.

47:27.928 --> 47:28.929
No.

47:31.139 --> 47:32.933
- Pardon?
- That's the result,

47:33.016 --> 47:35.269
but let's go with the first scenario.

47:35.852 --> 47:36.979
Are you sure?

47:37.604 --> 47:38.897
Yes.

47:38.981 --> 47:41.358
I already told Director General Ko.

47:43.235 --> 47:44.444
Director Jin.

47:44.528 --> 47:46.697
You know that
we'll all be reprimanded, right?

47:48.198 --> 47:51.034
Yes, I know. I'll take responsibility.

47:52.119 --> 47:54.246
Why would you take responsibility?

47:54.329 --> 47:56.415
If the typhoon deviates
from the expected course,

47:56.498 --> 47:59.293
I, the director of the typhoon center,
should take responsibility.

48:01.670 --> 48:03.088
Will you let me?

48:10.137 --> 48:12.889
All right.
Let's go with the first scenario.

48:14.182 --> 48:16.268
Good work, Director Jin.

48:16.351 --> 48:17.311
Good work.

48:26.695 --> 48:29.573
PRESS RELEASE

48:31.450 --> 48:32.451
Sorry?

48:32.534 --> 48:34.286
An excessive forecast?

48:35.412 --> 48:36.622
Yes.

48:36.705 --> 48:39.499
Director Jin wants to go
with the first scenario.

48:40.000 --> 48:42.836
If the effect of the northern jet stream
is weaker than expected,

48:42.919 --> 48:44.755
it'll move slower to the east.

48:44.838 --> 48:47.841
So let's prepare in case
it enters the southern inland of Korea.

48:48.425 --> 48:50.427
Still, is an excessive forecast necessary?

48:50.510 --> 48:52.054
The purpose of forecasting

48:52.137 --> 48:55.182
is to protect the lives
and safety of the people.

48:55.265 --> 48:57.934
I learned that being right
or wrong doesn't matter.

48:59.227 --> 49:01.146
All right, Director Jin.

49:01.229 --> 49:03.607
I'll tell the Office of Spokesperson
as ordered.

49:07.986 --> 49:10.322
TYPHOON ELISHA HEADING NORTH
TO THE SOUTHERN SEA OF JEJU

49:10.405 --> 49:12.658
EXPECTED TO HIT
THE SOUTHERN COAST AT DAWN

49:13.950 --> 49:14.910
News.

49:15.786 --> 49:17.162
News.

49:21.375 --> 49:22.417
News.

49:23.502 --> 49:24.461
Breaking news.

49:24.544 --> 49:27.214
Typhoon Elisha, the 15th typhoon,
which was heading north,

49:27.297 --> 49:29.758
is expected to go through
the Korean Peninsula

49:29.841 --> 49:32.761
starting from the southern coast
of South Jeolla Province at dawn tomorrow.

49:32.844 --> 49:34.680
According to the KMA,

49:34.763 --> 49:37.140
Typhoon Elisha is a strong typhoon

49:37.224 --> 49:39.685
with a central wind speed

49:39.768 --> 49:41.311
- of 30m per second.
- Bo-mi.

49:41.395 --> 49:43.313
Did you run home because of that?

49:44.189 --> 49:45.065
Yes.

49:45.148 --> 49:46.650
Because it's Dad's forecast.

49:48.610 --> 49:51.655
Since when have you been
so interested in your dad's work?

49:51.738 --> 49:54.950
The KMA added that people
should watch out for damage

49:55.033 --> 49:57.577
due to strong winds
and heavy rain overnight.

49:58.870 --> 50:00.122
- Assistant Director Shin.
- Yes.

50:00.205 --> 50:01.998
Give the statistics
to Assistant Director Oh.

50:02.082 --> 50:03.625
- And bring the data.
- Okay.

50:06.753 --> 50:09.464
Soo-jin, this is information
on the typhoon.

50:09.548 --> 50:10.966
- Oh, okay.
- Deliver it to them.

50:11.049 --> 50:12.134
Thank you.

50:17.180 --> 50:18.098
Like this.

50:27.607 --> 50:28.817
It's done.

50:29.901 --> 50:32.863
So are we going with the first scenario?

50:33.780 --> 50:34.906
Yes.

50:52.674 --> 50:54.843
It's my turn now.

50:56.261 --> 51:00.974
Which scenario should I choose
in breaking up with you?

51:02.267 --> 51:05.145
Scenario one. Cling to you.

51:08.565 --> 51:09.816
Scenario two.

51:10.400 --> 51:12.611
Break up on a high note.

51:15.238 --> 51:16.406
Scenario three.

51:17.324 --> 51:21.411
Drag it out as much as I can.

51:29.211 --> 51:31.838
So what's your decision?

51:39.387 --> 51:40.806
Give me a little more time.

52:07.749 --> 52:08.834
What is it?

52:09.543 --> 52:11.878
Did something go wrong at work?

52:13.421 --> 52:14.714
I don't think…

52:16.883 --> 52:18.260
I can do this.

52:19.469 --> 52:20.637
What do you mean?

52:20.720 --> 52:22.639
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

52:23.932 --> 52:27.894
I'm not good at focusing
on more than one thing.

52:28.603 --> 52:29.813
And?

52:29.896 --> 52:31.064
But…

52:31.815 --> 52:33.984
since I met you,

52:34.693 --> 52:37.737
I keep getting my priorities mixed up.

52:37.821 --> 52:38.822
But…

52:39.406 --> 52:41.408
I shouldn't do that at the KMA.

52:41.491 --> 52:43.910
What was your priority before?

52:44.661 --> 52:46.955
It was the KMA and the weather, of course.

52:47.038 --> 52:49.499
What is it now?

53:00.135 --> 53:00.969
Me?

53:04.723 --> 53:06.099
Normally…

53:06.975 --> 53:09.311
I'm not like this.

53:09.394 --> 53:10.353
Okay?

53:10.437 --> 53:14.900
I mean, I have never
mixed business with pleasure.

53:14.983 --> 53:17.277
I have never broken those rules

53:17.944 --> 53:20.030
because I'm rational and logical.

53:20.113 --> 53:22.449
- But…
- But what?

53:24.409 --> 53:26.536
Now I'm having an identity crisis.

53:28.663 --> 53:32.125
I don't know what to do
with this unpredictable feeling.

53:32.626 --> 53:36.171
If I make a big mistake,
it'll cause great public interest damages.

53:36.254 --> 53:38.006
Then I'll be terribly ashamed.

53:38.089 --> 53:40.008
I'll regret what I did and feel dejected.

53:40.091 --> 53:42.552
- Then I'll--
- Mr. Shin Seok-ho!

53:42.636 --> 53:43.637
Yes?

54:02.238 --> 54:03.782
I like you too.

54:07.619 --> 54:08.703
Really?

54:11.790 --> 54:12.832
Do you want dinner?

54:12.916 --> 54:16.127
Let's have mung bean pancakes
with rice wine.

54:16.211 --> 54:17.337
Let's go.

54:23.927 --> 54:25.553
Wait for me, Tae-kyung.

54:31.476 --> 54:32.394
Tae-kyung!

54:56.501 --> 54:58.169
- Nice!
- Yes!

54:58.253 --> 55:00.338
I wish I can
get the answers right like this.

55:00.422 --> 55:03.091
Exactly.
You're hitting them really well today.

55:11.182 --> 55:13.226
- Let me go again.
- Sure.

55:13.309 --> 55:15.478
- I have spare change.
- You're good today.

55:24.029 --> 55:26.197
What are you doing here?

55:27.073 --> 55:28.867
What brings you here?

55:29.451 --> 55:31.369
I told you it was Dad.

55:31.453 --> 55:33.663
I saw him come here.

55:33.747 --> 55:35.874
He was here yesterday and the day before.

55:35.957 --> 55:38.001
Right, Dad? I got you, right?

55:55.393 --> 55:57.854
You have three scenarios.

55:59.147 --> 56:00.356
"Scenarios"?

56:00.940 --> 56:01.900
First.

56:02.525 --> 56:03.693
Go back to work.

56:04.319 --> 56:06.112
- Honey.
- Second.

56:06.905 --> 56:08.198
Get divorced.

56:09.324 --> 56:11.159
- Honey.
- Third.

56:11.242 --> 56:12.994
Study like your life depends on it.

56:20.627 --> 56:23.880
Do you think I like supporting you?

56:23.963 --> 56:26.508
Because you said it was your dream,
I gave you a chance

56:27.342 --> 56:29.427
to give it a try before it was too late.

56:30.095 --> 56:31.888
So you wouldn't have any regrets.

56:31.971 --> 56:34.849
I thought this could be your last chance,

56:35.433 --> 56:37.352
so I let you study

56:37.435 --> 56:39.687
even though I was really tired.

56:40.396 --> 56:41.815
What did you say?

56:42.649 --> 56:44.275
Stressed out from studying?

56:51.616 --> 56:55.203
Don't you feel sorry at all
for making such excuses?

56:55.286 --> 56:57.038
Don't you feel sorry towards our kids?

57:05.046 --> 57:07.215
Don't you know your mom is suffering too?

57:07.298 --> 57:09.884
She's too old
to take care of those boys every day.

57:15.723 --> 57:16.808
Myung-ju.

57:17.350 --> 57:18.852
I'm sorry.

57:19.978 --> 57:21.354
I made a huge mistake.

57:25.608 --> 57:26.693
Make a choice.

57:27.861 --> 57:29.237
Is it scenario one,

57:29.821 --> 57:30.864
two, or three?

57:40.206 --> 57:43.376
I can't believe it. That's so stupid.

57:43.460 --> 57:46.087
Typhoon Elisha, the 15th typhoon,
which was expected to hit Korea

57:46.171 --> 57:47.714
early this morning,

57:47.797 --> 57:50.467
- Bo-mi. Were you here all night?
- passed through the South Sea

57:50.550 --> 57:53.511
- at 4 a.m.
- I don't know. I'm so mad.

57:53.595 --> 57:55.513
- What's wrong?
- Currently the typhoon

57:55.597 --> 57:57.265
- The forecast.
- is still active.

57:57.348 --> 57:59.559
Around 11 a.m., it'll weaken
due to the extratropical cyclone

57:59.642 --> 58:01.060
and then gradually disappear.

58:01.644 --> 58:05.690
Contrary to the KMA's prediction
that the typhoon would hit the inland…

58:05.773 --> 58:07.442
Is that it?

58:07.525 --> 58:09.527
Why did he get it wrong?

58:09.611 --> 58:11.946
He was right on the nose with Number 14.

58:12.572 --> 58:14.491
So what if the forecast was wrong?

58:14.574 --> 58:17.744
I'm glad there was no damage
even though it was wrong.

58:21.456 --> 58:22.415
What?

58:23.166 --> 58:24.584
Goosebumps.

58:25.585 --> 58:26.794
What was that, Mom?

58:26.878 --> 58:29.172
I thought there was nothing left
between you two

58:29.255 --> 58:31.174
because you were apart for so long.

58:31.257 --> 58:32.383
And?

58:32.467 --> 58:34.344
You sound like you work for the KMA.

58:35.762 --> 58:38.097
Stop being silly and get ready for school.

58:38.181 --> 58:39.557
I'll make breakfast.

58:43.561 --> 58:44.771
Honey.

58:45.897 --> 58:46.773
Bo-mi.

58:47.357 --> 58:48.816
I brought hangover soup.

58:49.442 --> 58:50.777
Hangover soup?

58:50.860 --> 58:51.945
What?

58:52.028 --> 58:53.780
You used to love it when you were little.

58:55.490 --> 58:56.866
That was a long time ago.

58:56.950 --> 58:59.369
I know. That restaurant
is still in business.

58:59.953 --> 59:01.037
It's really busy.

59:01.120 --> 59:04.332
Did you have breakfast?
Don't cook. Let's eat this.

59:04.415 --> 59:05.416
Come.

59:07.627 --> 59:11.339
I asked them for a lot of clotted blood.

59:12.549 --> 59:13.800
You like it, right?

59:13.883 --> 59:16.427
It smells great.

59:17.136 --> 59:19.847
Doesn't it? I need a bowl.

59:19.931 --> 59:21.307
- They're here.
- Okay.

59:21.975 --> 59:23.601
We need spoons too.

59:26.396 --> 59:27.730
Wait a minute.

59:29.232 --> 59:30.358
Is there enough space?

59:31.568 --> 59:33.861
Sure, you can place them there.

59:33.945 --> 59:35.196
We just need spoons.

01:00:24.245 --> 01:00:26.164
I can't believe them.

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.511
Put this on.

01:00:55.318 --> 01:00:56.486
How is your eye?

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:02.742
I think it's okay.

01:01:03.368 --> 01:01:05.620
You didn't have to follow me to the boat.

01:01:08.539 --> 01:01:09.582
I told you.

01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:12.210
You need experience to float a sonde.

01:01:15.171 --> 01:01:16.339
Also…

01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.758
I had the same idea as you.

01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:23.513
I thought Typhoon Elisha would
move to the eastern outskirts of Korea.

01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.060
I came out here

01:01:29.602 --> 01:01:31.104
just to check it for myself.

01:01:35.650 --> 01:01:37.110
Will you be all right?

01:01:40.822 --> 01:01:42.615
After breaking up with me,

01:01:42.699 --> 01:01:44.492
will you be able to work with me?

01:01:47.370 --> 01:01:50.456
Will you be okay, Director Jin?

01:02:02.385 --> 01:02:03.386
I'll be fine.

01:02:05.930 --> 01:02:07.390
I'll be okay.

01:02:11.519 --> 01:02:12.895
Let's break up.

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:21.237
Let's break up, Si-woo.

01:02:35.501 --> 01:02:36.586
Okay.

01:02:48.514 --> 01:02:50.558
The cause of typhoons

01:02:50.641 --> 01:02:53.186
is to resolve the thermal imbalance

01:02:53.269 --> 01:02:55.772
caused by the rotation of the Earth.

01:02:58.733 --> 01:03:02.779
Contrary to the KMA's prediction
that the typhoon would hit the inland,

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:04.655
it passed without much damage.

01:03:04.739 --> 01:03:07.408
- As a result, confidence
- I'm sorry.

01:03:07.492 --> 01:03:11.078
- in the KMA's forecast has fallen.
- Yes, I checked it.

01:03:11.579 --> 01:03:12.914
KMA'S TYPHOON MIS-FORECAST

01:03:12.997 --> 01:03:14.123
SHAMEFUL TYPHOON WARNING

01:03:14.207 --> 01:03:15.041
Well…

01:03:15.124 --> 01:03:17.084
YOU SAID THE TYPHOON WAS COMING!
WHERE IS ELISHA?

01:03:19.796 --> 01:03:20.755
Yes.

01:03:21.756 --> 01:03:24.801
Yes. I'll report to you again.

01:03:29.305 --> 01:03:30.431
Jeez.

01:03:34.727 --> 01:03:36.979
STOP EXCESSIVE FORECASTS.
WE WANT AN ACCURATE WEATHER REPORT.

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:42.193
This typhoon may be hard on us right now…

01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:52.662
but in the long run,

01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:56.082
it'll be beneficial to everyone.

01:04:16.644 --> 01:04:17.728
If only…

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:21.983
we could get through this moment.

01:04:25.152 --> 01:04:28.239
DOMESTIC FLIGHTS

01:04:43.337 --> 01:04:44.630
See you in the office.

01:04:48.467 --> 01:04:50.052
What should I do with your stuff?

01:04:51.053 --> 01:04:52.179
Oh, right…

01:04:52.263 --> 01:04:54.223
I'll take them on my next day off.

01:04:56.100 --> 01:04:57.143
Okay.

01:04:58.769 --> 01:04:59.812
All right.

01:05:34.513 --> 01:05:37.350
Why are you standing there like that?
This is your house.

01:06:08.923 --> 01:06:13.386
LIQUID IRON SUPPLEMENT FOR PREGNANT WOMEN

01:06:13.469 --> 01:06:16.055
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:06:18.557 --> 01:06:21.018
- Enjoy your lunch.
- Enjoy your lunch.

01:06:25.690 --> 01:06:26.565
Si-woo.

01:06:28.526 --> 01:06:30.111
Hello.

01:06:33.739 --> 01:06:36.492
I heard you're dating Director Jin.

01:06:37.743 --> 01:06:38.744
What?

01:06:38.828 --> 01:06:41.330
I'm so sorry

01:06:41.414 --> 01:06:43.249
I came between you two.

01:06:43.332 --> 01:06:44.917
It must have been uncomfortable.

01:06:45.001 --> 01:06:46.961
Were you already dating
when we stayed at her place?

01:06:48.546 --> 01:06:51.507
Where did you hear that from?

01:06:51.590 --> 01:06:53.217
It wasn't from anyone specific.

01:06:53.300 --> 01:06:55.678
Everyone on our team knew except me.

01:06:56.554 --> 01:06:58.389
Everyone?

01:06:58.472 --> 01:06:59.765
Everyone.

01:07:00.349 --> 01:07:02.685
By the way, you're so daring.

01:07:02.768 --> 01:07:04.353
I can't believe you're having

01:07:04.437 --> 01:07:07.773
an office romance
with none other than Director Jin.

01:07:07.857 --> 01:07:09.734
Forecaster Lee is dating Director Jin.

01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:11.360
- Is Director Jin dating someone at work?
- You know what?

01:07:11.444 --> 01:07:14.113
- Since when?
- I'm really happy for you.

01:07:15.281 --> 01:07:18.117
You two look great together.

01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:20.453
I'm sincerely happy for you.

01:07:21.495 --> 01:07:23.080
I also feel bad

01:07:23.622 --> 01:07:25.499
because I've been so slow-witted.

01:07:25.583 --> 01:07:27.209
Director Jin is dating that guy.

01:07:27.293 --> 01:07:29.211
Director Jin sure got it going on.

01:07:29.295 --> 01:07:31.756
- I'm jealous.
- I'm so jealous.

01:07:31.839 --> 01:07:33.049
- She's got everything.
- She's competent.

01:07:33.132 --> 01:07:34.633
Congratulations!

01:07:59.366 --> 01:08:01.368
Director Jin!

01:08:11.754 --> 01:08:13.089
Are you here for your stuff?

01:08:13.172 --> 01:08:15.257
I said I'd bring it to you. Wait here.

01:08:15.341 --> 01:08:17.093
There's a problem.

01:08:17.718 --> 01:08:18.719
What problem?

01:08:18.803 --> 01:08:20.596
They found out.

01:08:21.680 --> 01:08:22.765
Found out what?

01:08:22.848 --> 01:08:24.475
That we dated.

01:08:25.392 --> 01:08:26.227
What?

01:08:26.310 --> 01:08:28.437
Everyone on our team found out

01:08:28.521 --> 01:08:31.065
that you and I dated.

01:08:31.148 --> 01:08:32.358
What?

01:08:32.942 --> 01:08:33.984
You scared me.

01:08:38.322 --> 01:08:41.283
I knew it.

01:08:41.867 --> 01:08:42.743
So that means

01:08:42.827 --> 01:08:46.038
- you two dated at work. Is that right?
- Mom, that's--

01:08:46.122 --> 01:08:49.291
I knew there was something going on.

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:52.962
- It's a misunderstanding.
- Misunderstanding, my foot.

01:08:56.674 --> 01:08:58.968
I knew you'd deny it.

01:08:59.051 --> 01:09:01.887
So I got evidence.

01:09:09.019 --> 01:09:10.479
Will you deny it?

01:09:10.563 --> 01:09:11.939
Will you still deny it?

01:09:59.820 --> 01:10:03.616
People are taking it
more seriously than they should.

01:10:03.699 --> 01:10:06.577
Ignore them.
Don't listen to them or reply.

01:10:06.660 --> 01:10:08.913
But I made dumpling soup, your favorite.

01:10:08.996 --> 01:10:10.497
- Are you ill?
- I just have a stomachache.

01:10:10.581 --> 01:10:12.583
I thought he'd be much more mature.

01:10:12.666 --> 01:10:13.709
But he turned out to be a baby.

01:10:13.792 --> 01:10:15.211
You must really love him.

01:10:15.294 --> 01:10:17.296
We broke up.

01:10:17.880 --> 01:10:20.507
You can't maintain
a relationship if it's one-sided.

01:10:21.217 --> 01:10:22.134
Where should we go?

01:10:23.093 --> 01:10:24.762
I have something to tell you.

01:10:24.845 --> 01:10:28.641
To be honest, Forecaster Lee and I…

01:10:28.724 --> 01:10:32.811
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
